{
    // CommonJS half of the published `dist/` (see tools/build-ts.mjs).
    //
    // Three options have to move together with `module: CommonJS` and none of
    // them is cosmetic:
    //   * `moduleResolution: bundler` — this one is pinned to the COMPILER
    //     MAJOR, not chosen on its merits, so do not "tidy" it. TypeScript 7
    //     removed `node10` outright (TS5108), and it refuses `node16` beside a
    //     CommonJS `module` (TS5110, "module must be set to Node16"), which
    //     leaves `bundler` as the only resolution mode TS 7 will pair with a
    //     CommonJS emit. It is resolution only — `module: CommonJS` is what
    //     decides the emit, and the `./types.js` specifiers gen/ts writes
    //     resolve fine under it. The pairing is rejected by TS <= 6 (TS5095),
    //     so this line and the `typescript` pin in package.json move in
    //     lock-step; CI fails loudly on any mismatch rather than silently
    //     emitting the wrong module system.
    //   * `verbatimModuleSyntax: false` — with it on, tsc rejects `export` in a
    //     file it is about to emit as CommonJS (TS1286) rather than
    //     down-levelling it, which is exactly what this pass exists to do.
    //   * `dist/cjs/package.json` carries `"type": "commonjs"` (written by
    //     tools/build-ts.mjs) — the root package is `"type": "module"`, so
    //     without that marker Node parses these `.js` files as ESM and every
    //     `require()` dies on `exports is not defined`.
    //
    // Not `module: node16`, which is the obvious-looking replacement for the
    // removed `node10`: under node16 tsc derives each file's module system from
    // the package.json nearest the SOURCE, and gen/ts sits under this
    // repository's `"type": "module"` root, so it emits ESM into dist/cjs/ and
    // `require()` dies on `Unexpected token 'export'`. Writing dist/cjs/package.json
    // before tsc runs does not help: the marker beside the OUTPUT is not what
    // node16 reads. tests/consumer/run.sh is what catches this.
    "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
    "compilerOptions": {
        "noEmit": false,
        "declaration": true,
        "declarationMap": false,
        "sourceMap": false,
        "outDir": "dist/cjs",
        "rootDir": "gen/ts",
        "module": "CommonJS",
        "moduleResolution": "bundler",
        "verbatimModuleSyntax": false,
        "newLine": "lf",
        "incremental": false
    },
    "include": ["gen/ts/**/*.ts"]
}
